==============================================================================
[2] the two failure modes respond differently
==============================================================================
  arm                                      median         failures > 5 %
  state mask + plume|test_id       0.7 ->   0.4 %           16 ->     4 %
  state mask + plume|test_ood      0.8 ->   0.8 %           36 ->    20 %
  state mask only|test_id         26.8 ->  19.1 %          100 ->    83 %

  Out of distribution with the plume, restarting removes 44 % of
  the failures, because they were the optimiser losing an answer that was
  present in the data.

  With masks alone it changes the failure rate from 100 % to 83 %.
  Selecting by misfit cannot work when every candidate has the same misfit.
  A better optimiser does not buy information that is not there.

